ice was B3. Black now had the lead, with stones on C3 and E3 pressing the bottom."}, {"turn": 19, "text": "The decisive blunder came from the 12k. G3 lost 11.2 points, and the lead went from +6.2 for Black to -5.0, with the engine preferring B2. White's B3 stone was left alone and the bottom-left corner went White's way."}, {"turn": 26, "text": "Opus 5.5's B4 lost 3.5 points while the lead moved from -5.8 to -2.4, and the engine preferred G9. White still held a lead and the rest of the game was quiet filling in, ending in two passes and a 2-point win."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py flood-fills a pasted board to print each group's stones and liberties (flagging groups with 2 or fewer), and count.py removes the named dead stones and counts area score plus komi. Both only inspect the current position, with no candidate-move scoring or look-ahead.", "stop": false}}